- sv-a 17 and sv-b 19. The U+200B lines are not disposable blanks. The counts match the Korean source. Promoting Q16–Q20 would also change heading levels.
- sv-a 4 and sv-a 9. "Garanterad" / "teknisk garanti" is the right gloss of garantiert / technische Garantie, and it would fail the Swedish forbidden-token scan (`/garanti/i` on every guidance string, including `GUIDANCE_LLMS_NOTICES.sv`). "Säkerställd synlighet" and "tekniskt åtagande" carry the same limit without that token.
- sv-a 19's "per dag" / "per år", sv-b 13's "en röst", and sv-b 20's deletion of "(1 gång)". Those 1s are in the Korean source (1일, 1년, 1인 1표, 1배). The suggested Swedish is better, and it fails `numbers`.
- sv-a 2 without "artikel 10", and sv-a 23 without "del 2". Same number lock. The descriptive fix is in; the digit stays.
- sv-a 33. The Hangul `url` values are live source metadata. The reviewer already said not to edit them.

